-- A member has a loan when a Loan exists for it. Nothing deletes a Loan, and rule MoveLoan
-- gives a loan to another member by setting the loan's `member`.
--
-- The state-flow diagram for Member says entry to MemberWithLoan is permanent, with the note
-- "exists Loan for this can never stop holding", and also draws an arrow out of
-- MemberWithLoan caused by MoveLoan. The arrow is right: a member whose only loan moves away
-- stops being a MemberWithLoan. The note is wrong.
act Member { name: text }

act Loan {
    member: one Member
    dueOn: Date
}

transient act Transfer {
    loan: one Loan
    receiver: one Member
}

rule MoveLoan when Transfer {
    loan.member = receiver
}

shape MemberWithLoan = Member where exists Loan for this
